<Section id="teaching" title="Teaching">
  <p>
    Growing up, I was lucky to have access to some amazing maths educators.
    Over the years I have seen many students -- from primary school to university -- being forced to memorise seemingly useless facts and being told that they are not good enough, removing all the joy from learning.
    I want to give back to the community by sparking students' curiosity and letting them discover beautiful ideas for themselves.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>I have been teaching algorithmic programming to students aged 10-18, from the basics up to olympiad preparation.</li>
    <li>I have successfully prepared several students for end-of-year and high-school-leaving maths exams.</li>
    <li>I was a teaching assistant at ETH Zürich for courses like Computational Intelligence Lab or Advanced Algorithms.</li>
    <li>I am a volunteer at <a href="https://indahousehungary.hu/">InDaHouse</a>, teaching maths and English to Hungarian children from disadvantaged backgrounds.</li>
  </ul>
</Section>